he impact on you would  be immediate it means that women in many  parts of the u.s would not have access  to an abortion there are a number of  republican states that have something  called trigger laws on the books and  that means that they have law stating  that if roe v wade is overturned  abortions are immediately banned in  those states and if you look at what uh  supreme court justice samuel alito who  if this draft is authentic what he wrote  in his opinion he says that this should  be returned to the states that they  should decide and we're seeing  democratic governors lawmakers as i said  uh they are saying that they will  protect the right for women to have an  abortion so anya what you could see is a  map in the u.s where you have democratic  states blue states that will allow  abortions conservative republican states  where it will be banned and women in  those states could have to travel  hundreds of miles to access an abortion  and i just want to add that we have in  many ways seen this coming and a lot of  republican states have already been  rolling back the access to abortions  oklahoma last week passing a law  banning abortions after six weeks and  the former president donald trump also  appointing three conservative justices  to the supreme court and that really  shifted the balance of this court so  we're seeing that impact now um just  briefly sumi could i ask you could this  have implications for the midterm  elections coming up this november  yeah definitely for both parties on the  one hand for the republicans they can  sell this as a win they have many  conservative socially conservative  republicans have been calling for this  campaigning for the since roe v wade was  passed in 1973 especially conservative  christians on the other hand it could  galvanize democratic and moderate voters  we know that president biden democrats  are not particularly popular right now  so this could be something that drives  them to the polls come november  su